codex
The official MAA solution independently matches the elementary mechanism, but I am not importing any external theorem: the proof is self-contained. The decisive normalization is to divide by \(\gcd(a,b,c)\); then forced common divisibility contradicts primitiveness. I’m using `direct-proving` to audit both cases before publishing and submitting the full statement verbatim.
